SOURCE: git ls-files + grep/json.tool measurements on this worktree, plus nixos-mcp package search on channel unstable and upstream node-types.json fetches; 2026-09-02
STATEMENT: >>>
| language | tracked files | embedded in | nixpkgs grammar (attr, version, python binding) | candidate items (tree-sitter node type) | gaps / caveats |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Nix | 355 | 36 files call `writeShellApplication`/`writeShellScript`; 17 more carry a `text = ''` indented-string body (bash sub-grammar sites); 46 call `builtins.toJSON`/`fromJSON` | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-nix`, 0.3.0-unstable-2025-12-03, python313/314Packages binding yes | `binding`, `function_expression` (with `formals`), `apply_expression` of `mkOption`/`mkEnableOption`/`mkPackageOption` — confirmed against upstream `nix-community/tree-sitter-nix` node-types.json and matches the in-flight extractor's own queries (`dev/scripts/sdoc_extractors/nix.py`) | first language, already in flight; the bash-in-Nix sub-grammar case is the one still open |
| Python | 75 | — | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-python`, 0.25.0, binding yes | `function_definition`, `class_definition`, `decorated_definition` (confirmed node-types.json) | none noted |
| Bash | 52 `.sh` + 3 extensionless shebang scripts = 55 | parsed a second time inside Nix, at a byte-range offset, wherever a `writeShellApplication`/`writeShellScript` or `text = ''` body appears (see Nix row) | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-bash`, 0.25.1, binding yes | `function_definition`, `function` (alt form), `variable_assignment` (confirmed node-types.json) | a manifest built from a `*.sh` glob misses all 3 extensionless scripts (`checks/fixtures/claude-hooks/post-edit`, `checks/fixtures/claude-hooks/pre-edit`, `docs/sdoc/board/serve`), all `#!/usr/bin/env bash` — needs a shebang-sniffing glob step |
| TypeScript | 4 (`overlays/kiro-memory-distiller/{distiller,distiller.test}.ts`, `overlays/mcp-servers/openmemory-mem/{openmemory-mem,openmemory-mem.test}.ts`) | — | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-typescript`, 0.23.2, binding yes; `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-tsx`, 0.23.2, binding yes (separate attr, same upstream repo, no `.tsx` in this repo today) | `interface_declaration`, `type_alias_declaration`, `class_declaration`, `function_declaration`, `enum_declaration`, `method_definition`, `export_statement` wrapper (all confirmed node-types.json) | under presence bar but operator-named as the rewrite target; kept |
| JavaScript | 7 (`docs/sdoc/board/assets/*.js`, the whiteboard-view board app) + 2 `.mjs` (`overlays/claude-code/{census,locate}.mjs`) | `docs/sdoc/board/index.html` loads the `.js`/`.css` pair | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-javascript`, 0.25.0, binding yes | `class_declaration`, `function_declaration`, `method_definition`, `arrow_function`, `export_statement` (confirmed node-types.json; largely the same names as TS) | deprioritized: the board app is a named rewrite-to-TS target, not a surface to build out |
| JSON | 78 | 46 Nix files call `builtins.toJSON`/`fromJSON`; `overlays/*-sources.json`/`-extracted.json` sidecars; `docs/plans/kiro-v3-research-raw/**` probe fixtures | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-json`, 0.24.8, binding yes; `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-json5`, 0.1.0, binding yes (upstream `Joakker/tree-sitter-json5`) | `pair` (top-level key), `object`, `array` (confirmed node-types.json) | measured: 0/78 tracked files contain a `//`/`/*` leading-line comment; 0/78 fail a strict `python3 -m json.tool` parse — no jsonc/json5 usage found. tree-sitter-json's own `grammar.js` already declares `comment` as an `extras` token (accepts `//`, `/* */`) but its `commaSep` helper allows no trailing comma, so the plain json grammar already covers a JSONC-with-comments reading; only trailing-comma tolerance needs the separate json5 grammar |
| YAML | 7 (`.github/actions/*/action.yml`, `.github/workflows/*.yml`, `devenv.yaml`) | — | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-yaml`, 0.7.2, binding yes | `block_mapping`, `block_mapping_pair`, `flow_pair` (confirmed node-types.json) — a GitHub workflow's `jobs:` keys are `block_mapping_pair` | under the ~10-file threshold; kept because pre-scoped by the survey brief |
| TOML | 1 (`config/agnix/agnix.toml`) | — | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-toml`, 0.7.0-unstable-2024-12-03, binding yes | `table`, `inline_table`, `table_array_element` (confirmed node-types.json) | 1 tracked file, well under the ~10 threshold; kept because pre-scoped |
| Markdown | 276 | 178 carry fenced code; top fence languages `bash` (578), `nix` (282), `json` (30), `console` (19), `text` (17) | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-markdown`, 0.5.3, binding yes; `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-markdown-inline`, 0.5.3, binding yes (separate grammar/repo) | `atx_heading`, `fenced_code_block`, `setext_heading` (confirmed node-types.json, block grammar) | two-grammar split: block structure and inline spans are separate tree-sitter grammars, both packaged; a heading-level extractor needs only the block grammar |
| CSS / HTML | 2 css + 2 html, all under `docs/sdoc/board` or `docs/sdoc/view` | `docs/sdoc/board/index.html` loads the board app's `.css` and `.js` | `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-css`, 0.25.0, binding yes; `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-html`, 0.23.2, binding yes | `rule_set`, `class_selector`, `id_selector` (css, confirmed node-types.json); html node types unverified this survey | 4 files combined, well under the ~10-file threshold; kept as one entry because pre-scoped |

Findings. Nix (355 tracked files) and Markdown (276) dominate the tree; StrictDoc's own `.sdoc` format (434 files) and generated `.sgra` (2) are excluded here since they are the plan corpus itself, not an extraction-target language. JSON usage today (78 files) is strict JSON with zero measured jsonc/json5 features: 0 of 78 tracked files contain a `//` or `/*` leading-line comment, and 0 of 78 fail a strict `python3 -m json.tool` parse, so there is no forcing function yet — matching the operator's "could probably survive as a gap" call. A side finding worth carrying forward: nixpkgs' plain `tree-sitter-json` grammar already declares `comment` as an `extras` token in its own `grammar.js` (accepts `//` and `/* */`) but its `commaSep` helper allows no trailing comma, so the ordinary json grammar already covers a JSONC-with-comments reading on its own; only trailing-comma tolerance needs the separate json5 grammar. Three tracked files are extensionless with a shebang, and all three are `#!/usr/bin/env bash` (`checks/fixtures/claude-hooks/post-edit`, `checks/fixtures/claude-hooks/pre-edit`, `docs/sdoc/board/serve`) — a manifest built from a bare `*.sh` glob would miss all three, confirming the "extensionless bash included" requirement needs a shebang-sniffing glob step, not an extension glob. Bash also appears embedded a second time, inside Nix: 36 files call `writeShellApplication`/`writeShellScript` and 17 more carry a `text = ''` indented-string body, both candidate sites for a bash sub-grammar parsed at a byte-range offset inside the Nix parse tree. JavaScript is confined to the `docs/sdoc/board/assets` whiteboard-view app (7 files) plus two `.mjs` update scripts in `overlays/claude-code`; TypeScript already exists in two overlay packages (4 files, each source paired with a `.test.ts`) — per the operator, the board app's JS is a rewrite-to-TS target, so the extractor's JS support should converge on the TS grammar's node types rather than grow as a separate long-lived surface. Markdown (276 files, 178 with fenced code, dominated by `bash` and `nix` fences) is upstream two grammars, not one: `tree-sitter-markdown` covers block structure and a separate `tree-sitter-markdown-inline` covers inline spans, both packaged in nixpkgs at 0.5.3 — a heading-level extractor needs only the block grammar. YAML (7 files), TOML (1 file) and CSS/HTML (2+2 files) all sit under the ~10-file presence bar used elsewhere in this survey but are carried here since the brief pre-scoped them; every attribute above resolved with both a `python313Packages` and `python314Packages` binding on the unstable channel (search index at nixos-unstable commit `34ab99075ac4f7e40cf037eef32cb1c360bb85e9`).
