NOTES: >>>
DEPTH implemented, not verified: this is a one-pass survey, not an
independently re-run observation — the corpus convention here (see the other
`EV-` nodes in this plan) is `implemented` for a completed measurement session
and `verified` only once a second session re-runs it.

Filed 2026-09-02 against this worktree (`nix-agentic-tools-worktrees/strictdoc-trial`)
and the live nixpkgs search index at channel `unstable`
(commit `34ab99075ac4f7e40cf037eef32cb1c360bb85e9`, via the nixos-mcp tool); the
repo's own `flake.lock` pins `nixpkgs-src` to `NixOS/nixpkgs` at
`c8f90650c15282fa8656a041bfbbd2403997a9a7` (lastModified 1787394516).

Commands run (from the worktree root):

```bash
git ls-files | sed -n 's/.*\.\([^./]*\)$/\1/p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn
git ls-files | wc -l
git ls-files | while read -r f; do case "$f" in *.*) ;; *) [ -f "$f" ] && \
  [ "$(head -c2 -- "$f")" = "#!" ] && head -n1 -- "$f";; esac; done
git grep -lE 'writeShellApplication|writeShellScript' -- '*.nix' | wc -l
git grep -lE "text = ''" -- '*.nix' | wc -l
git grep -hE '^```[a-zA-Z0-9_+-]+' -- '*.md' \
  | sed -E 's/^```([a-zA-Z0-9_+-]+).*/\1/' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn
git grep -lE '^\s*(//|/\*)' -- '*.json'
git ls-files '*.json' | while read -r f; do python3 -m json.tool -- "$f" >/dev/null || echo "FAIL: $f"; done
git grep -lE 'builtins\.(to|from)JSON' -- '*.nix' | wc -l
```

Grammar lookups: `mcp__plugin_hm_nixos-mcp__nix` (`action: search`,
`query: tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-<lang>`, `type: packages`) for every
row's attribute and version; `python31{3,4}Packages.tree-sitter-grammars.*`
confirmed present alongside every attr queried, so "python binding: yes" is
uniform across the table and not called out per row beyond that.

Node types were confirmed by fetching each grammar's `src/node-types.json`
from its upstream GitHub repo (`nix-community/tree-sitter-nix`,
`tree-sitter/tree-sitter-{python,bash,json,javascript,typescript,css}`,
`tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-yaml`,
`tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-toml`,
`tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-markdown` split_parser branch) rather than
guessed from memory; HTML's node types were not fetched (time-boxed) and are
marked unverified in the table. `Joakker/tree-sitter-json5` was located as the
upstream for nixpkgs' `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-json5` by trying
candidate org/repo names against raw.githubusercontent.com until one 200'd;
its own node-types.json was not fetched.

The in-flight Nix extractor's own tree-sitter queries
(`dev/scripts/sdoc_extractors/nix.py:100-124`) were cross-checked against the
upstream node-types.json rather than trusted standalone, and match: `binding`,
`function_expression`/`formals`, `apply_expression` with an `mkOption` /
`mkEnableOption` / `mkPackageOption` function-name match.
